<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The card the logo is printed on, sampled from art/logo.png.

        Written by scripts/generate-launcher-icons.py, which takes the
        median of every pixel of the card the mark does not touch — edit
        the logo rather than this number. It is the adaptive icon's
        background layer, and what the monogram was drawn to sit on: the
        artwork is letterpressed, so its highlights are lighter than the
        paper and only read as highlights against this exact colour.

        Not a night variant, and it must not become one. An icon that
        changed with the system theme would be a different icon on the
        same launcher twice a day. The splash screen, which does want to
        follow the theme, has its own colour in splash_background.xml.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#F1ECE1</color>
</resources>
